# The item 160 and 161 lines sit AFTER the lamps on purpose: a runtime older than item mode-leds
# reads only the first 16 KB of a port, and everything it understands must stay inside that.
# ---- item 160: the game's own rules, a shot that COUNTS AS one of theirs (MODE_SDK.md "Counts as") ------
# DESK ONLY on this build (read off its ELF 08d50299 by item 158's address pass; not run): the manager's
# get (cmp r1,#26; push {r3,lr}; the 27-entry table at 0x7a1698), the slots of this build (the shot
# handler v[41]: Premium 1.16 added a slot at 41 and has it at v[42]), the per-player lit mask at
# obj + 0x18 + 8 * player. The rule vtable pointers are the words the objects carry (ebirah's v[41]
# there is 0x7ff18, the tank's 0x107808, as item 158 located them by signature).
site stock_rule_get   0x000d1c10 0xe351001a 0xe92d4008
value stock_slot_shot   41
value stock_slot_active 14
value stock_slot_lit    25
value stock_field       0x18
rule 12 0x006266d0 Battle vs Ebirah
rule 4  0x00630100 Tank attack multiball
# ---- item 161: the game's own rules REWRITTEN in C (pad_stock.h; MODE_SDK.md "Rewriting a stock rule's shot logic") ----
# addresses are item 158's Pro 1.15 twins where it read them ("158") and the LE address minus the
# unit's offset where it did not (ebirah unit -0x17d0, tank unit -0x2838, cmode base -0x17c8: "delta",
# each checked against the Ghidra decompile of both builds for this item (the item's scratch folder):
# every twin's decompiled shape matches LE's at 0.97..1.00 token similarity, ghidra/twins.txt).
# Pro 1.15 has NOT run any of this. Words read from the ELF (sha1 08d50299) by port_words.py.
#
site caward_add       0x0002facc 0xe92d41f0 0xe1a04000  # 158 (stock_modes.ENGINE_PRO115)
site caward_build     0x0002f784 0xe92d4ff8 0xe1a0b000  # ENGINE_PRO115
site caward_add_scaled 0x0002fb8c 0xe92d4ff8 0xe1a09002  # ENGINE_PRO115
